1
00:00:00,110 --> 00:00:00,860
Hi there.

2
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:10,670
It's time to talk about skills, What type of skills are there and how to describe your skills using

3
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:11,480
adjectives.

4
00:00:11,480 --> 00:00:15,450
Words like smart, reliable, independent.

5
00:00:15,470 --> 00:00:16,400
Let's go.

6
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:17,300
Okay.

7
00:00:17,330 --> 00:00:24,720
Skill is the knowledge and ability that helps you to do something well.

8
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:26,050
I can swim.

9
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:29,830
That means that swimming is my skill.

10
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:35,170
So there are two major types of skills.

11
00:00:35,180 --> 00:00:37,850
First type hard skills.

12
00:00:37,850 --> 00:00:40,610
Second type soft skills.

13
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:41,750
Let's see.

14
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:44,870
What is the difference between these types?

15
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:45,520
Okay.

16
00:00:45,530 --> 00:00:47,000
Hard skills.

17
00:00:47,030 --> 00:00:53,840
This is something you can learn from school or previous work or experience.

18
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:57,170
You can easily measure hard skills.

19
00:00:57,170 --> 00:01:06,810
For example, you can measure your English level or your python skill and hard skills are more objective.

20
00:01:06,810 --> 00:01:09,000
It is easier to see them.

21
00:01:10,290 --> 00:01:10,830
Okay.

22
00:01:10,830 --> 00:01:15,120
Soft skills are also called people skills.

23
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:18,690
It is difficult to measure soft skills.

24
00:01:18,690 --> 00:01:25,310
For example, how can you measure someone's teamwork or level of responsibility?

25
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:30,450
And soft skills are not connected to a specific job.

26
00:01:30,750 --> 00:01:39,600
If you are good at communication, you will be good at it at any job and position.

27
00:01:40,630 --> 00:01:51,040
Okay, let's have a look at this part of a CV and decide what hard and soft skill does this person have.

28
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:57,760
Okay, So we can see it's a front end developer with more than three years of experience in software

29
00:01:57,760 --> 00:01:59,500
development industry.

30
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:06,930
A quick learning person who can absorb new ideas can communicate clearly and effectively.

31
00:02:06,940 --> 00:02:13,870
And this person knows Angular two, TypeScript Webpack since March 2016.

32
00:02:13,930 --> 00:02:17,740
Okay, so soft skills of this person.

33
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:26,500
He or she is a quick learner, open to new ideas and good communication skill.

34
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:28,770
Hard skills.

35
00:02:28,810 --> 00:02:30,160
Angular2.

36
00:02:30,190 --> 00:02:31,310
TypeScript.

37
00:02:31,330 --> 00:02:32,400
Webpack.

38
00:02:32,410 --> 00:02:35,920
And maybe we can add frontend development.

39
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:43,900
Okay, so we can use this words and phrases with the word skill.

40
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:52,270
So you can develop a skill, you can learn new skill, you can work on your skill, you can improve

41
00:02:52,270 --> 00:02:56,470
your skill, make it better, and you can measure your skill.

42
00:02:56,650 --> 00:03:00,640
Okay, Pause the video and repeat the phrases.

43
00:03:01,270 --> 00:03:02,140
Good job.

44
00:03:02,830 --> 00:03:06,790
Most popular soft skills in a workplace.

45
00:03:06,790 --> 00:03:15,550
So it's communication, teamwork, problem solving, time management, critical thinking, decision

46
00:03:15,550 --> 00:03:24,370
making, stress management, adaptability, conflict management, leadership and creativity.

47
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:28,420
Pause the video and repeat those skills.

48
00:03:28,780 --> 00:03:29,740
Nice.

49
00:03:30,070 --> 00:03:38,410
I highlighted communication, teamwork, and leadership because I think these are the key skills.

50
00:03:40,110 --> 00:03:44,250
Okay, let's learn how to describe soft skills.

51
00:03:44,250 --> 00:03:46,110
So this is John.

52
00:03:46,350 --> 00:03:50,670
John always takes responsibility for the team.

53
00:03:50,670 --> 00:03:59,330
We know we can rely on him so we can say that John is reliable because we can rely on him.

54
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:03,690
He is responsible because he takes responsibility.

55
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:10,500
We can say that John is a good leader and he's a good team player.

56
00:04:11,100 --> 00:04:12,030
All right.

57
00:04:14,450 --> 00:04:17,690
Let's have a look at this pictures.

58
00:04:17,810 --> 00:04:21,290
People are describing their soft skills.

59
00:04:21,290 --> 00:04:27,650
Let's read and try to guess what are the soft skills of these people.

60
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:37,580
One one of my strongest soft skills is skill because I like to deal with difficult customers.

61
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:44,150
Two, I think I am because I am always open to change.

62
00:04:44,810 --> 00:04:50,330
In my eyes, I am a great because I like working with others.

63
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:52,430
Do you have any ideas?

64
00:04:52,850 --> 00:04:54,620
Okay, let's check now.

65
00:04:56,180 --> 00:05:04,100
One of my strongest soft skills is problem solving because I like to deal with difficult customers.

66
00:05:04,430 --> 00:05:10,700
I think I'm adaptable because I'm always open to change in my eyes.

67
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:15,200
I am a great team player because I like working with others.

68
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:16,340
Have you guessed?

69
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:17,660
Great.

70
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:19,520
Okay.

71
00:05:19,530 --> 00:05:21,960
How to describe your skills?

72
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:24,600
What words and phrases to use.

73
00:05:24,870 --> 00:05:29,080
You can say I am and add an adjective.

74
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:32,070
For example, I am responsible.

75
00:05:32,250 --> 00:05:34,000
I am independent.

76
00:05:34,020 --> 00:05:36,780
I am a good team player.

77
00:05:36,810 --> 00:05:38,220
Good is adjective.

78
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:44,130
Or you can say I have experience with and add a noun.

79
00:05:44,160 --> 00:05:52,920
It's often used to describe your hard skills so you can say I have experience with databases, I have

80
00:05:52,920 --> 00:06:00,610
experience with PHP, or you can say I am good at and add a noun.

81
00:06:00,630 --> 00:06:03,360
You can say I am good at communication.

82
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:06,090
I am good at presentation.

83
00:06:06,090 --> 00:06:08,700
I am good at teamwork.

84
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:11,100
Good job, guys.

85
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:17,810
Go to your file, do all the tasks, and come back to this video if you need to refresh your memory.

86
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:19,460
Thank you and bye.
